# kernel-nds32.img -- Linux 5.15.128 for the Andes AE3XX (nds32le, N13)
#
# Runs on qemu-system-nds32 -M ae3xx from the qemu fork (lordrasmus/qemu,
# branch uclibc-ng); upstream qemu never had nds32.  The image is the
# stripped vmlinux (ELF), which carries physical load addresses.
#
#   qemu-system-nds32 -M ae3xx -nographic -kernel kernel-nds32.img \
#     -initrd rootfs.img.xz -append console=ttyS0
#
# The machine follows arch/nds32/boot/dts/ae3xx.dts and generates the
# device tree itself (UART at 0xf0300000, ATCPIT100 timer at 0xf0400000,
# 256 MiB from 0).  It also enters the initrd as /memreserve/, because
# arch/nds32 never calls reserve_initrd_mem().  No kernel patches.
#
# 5.15 is the last line with nds32 (removed in v5.18).  The same image
# serves the 5.10.217 and 5.15.128 targets.
#
# Build: kernel-nds32.config is the nds32 defconfig with DEVTMPFS(_MOUNT),
# RD_XZ, PRINTK_TIME and CPU_N13, and without DEBUG_INFO, MODULES, FPU,
# CACHE_L2 and the FTMAC100 Ethernet the machine does not model.
#
#   cd linux-5.15.128
#   cp kernel-nds32.config .config
#   make ARCH=nds32 CROSS_COMPILE=nds32le-openadk-linux-uclibc- \
#        olddefconfig vmlinux
#   nds32le-openadk-linux-uclibc-strip -o kernel-nds32.img vmlinux
#
# The toolchain is the CI's toolchain-nds32le-gcc-13.2.0-npt-shared.
#
# Known: each exiting process logs "BUG: non-zero pgtables_bytes on
# freeing mm: 4096", a page table accounting mismatch not tracked down
# yet (arch/nds32's own pgd_free is the suspect).  Harmless for the tests.
